ly if he was in talks to play mr.  fantastic or any other Marvel character  he would not be able to say but that  look definitely implies that he's up to  something and then we get the report a  day later that he's met with Marvel  Studios and this is more than just a  coincidence especially if you consider  the third thing that you need to know  which is that his wife Emily Blunt has  also met with Marvel Studios about a  role in the MCU it was revealed that  while Emily Blunt was filming Jungle  Cruise her movie coming out with the  rock also a Disney movie which Disney  owns Marvel she met with Marvel Studios  now we don't really know much about  anything that happened  this meeting besides the fact that it  was to talk about an upcoming project  that Marvel Studios was working on but  that now means that Marvel Studios has  met with both Emily Blunt and her  husband John Krasinski and there's no  doubt that Marvel Studios knows that the  fans want John Krasinski and Emily Blunt  to play mr. fantastic and The Invisible  Woman and it's very clear by John  Krasinski's YouTube video plus  interviews that he's done that he knows  fans want him to play that as well and  that brings us to the fourth thing that  you need to know that comes from a  report from Mikey Sutton and this is  what Mikey had to say even though  countless fans have been blowing up  social media to have John Krasinski in  the role that doesn't mean that the  studios will listen  however several insiders have told Mikey  such and that Krasinski is in serious  negotiations for mr. fantastic as for  his wife Emily Blunt who would make the  perfect Invisible Woman that is still up  in the air as she apparently isn't  interested in what a lengthy contract  would be however sources have told Mikey  that if Krasinski is cast as mr.  fantastic it's pretty much a sure thing  that blunt will come with him to play  The Invisible Woman and apparently  Marvel Studios is interested in  Krasinski beyond his acting abilities  and are actually looking at him to  direct a Marvel Studios film which we'll  talk about in number five number four is  that the timing of all of this seems to  really line up we recently found out  that Marvel Studios was planning for the  new MCU Fantastic Four to make their  debut in ant-man 3 along with this Paul  Rudd also wrote an entire script that  included modock in it apparently now  Marvel has moved away from this idea and  are thinking about including the young  Avengers in the film but they were  planning on introducing the Fantastic  Four but instead of them actually having  a pretty major role in the movie they'll  probably now be teased in the film which  means we can probably expect an actual  Fantastic Four movie to come out right  around then if not too long after and  Marvel Studios does have a tendency to  pick actors for roles before actual  scripts are done and before directors  are chosen for example they cast Maher  shala alleyway before anything for blade  has been done including script or  casting no directors no writers no one  but Maher Sheila Ali has been cast for  that film the same thing happened with  Captain Marvel they cast brie Larson way  before they had a director and Kevin  you did mention about blade when asked  why blade why now he said because of my  Hershel ollie  so perhaps John Krasinski and Emily  Blunt are just the perfect cast for mr.  fantastic and The Invisible Woman that  they fit so perfectly for the movie to  come out however the last thing you need  to know coming in at number 5 is that  John Krasinski could very well be  directing a Marvel Studios film yes  everybody wants John Krasinski and Emily  Blunt to play mr. fantastic and The  Invisible Woman  of course Marvel Studios knows this and  of course they'll take this into  consideration but just because they may  cast them as characters in the MCU  doesn't mean that they can't also have  John Krasinski direct an MCU film John  Krasinski has recen